SUMMARY:Book Launch: Against Tech Oligarchy
LOCATION:MIT\, 134 MASSACHUSETTS Avenue\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:In a new book Against Tech Oligarchy\, JS Tan — a current DUS
 P Phd student — writes about tech worker activism\, the shifting labor p
 olitics of Silicon Valley\, and the rise of today's tech oligarchs. In the
  AI age\, as tech's most powerful leaders unilaterally force the new techn
 ology upon its workers\, this book makes the case that workers — when un
 ited — can build the leverage to push back\; and even fight for more equ
 itable and socially just ways to use the technology. Join JS Tan and his c
 o-author at this upcoming event for a conversation on these topics and to 
 celebrate the launch of their book.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/book-l
 aunch-against-tech-oligarchy\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/bo
 ston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/book-launch-against-tech-oligarchy
END:VEVENT
